# Manual-action handoffs

For all Aedrova work, proactively tell the owner whenever they must personally act.
State the exact action, where to do it, why it is needed, what it unlocks, and whether
it blocks the current milestone. Distinguish required-now steps from later setup.
Do not bury required actions solely in linked documentation. Include them in the
user-facing response and keep the setup documentation current.
Do not claim an integration is complete when accounts, migrations, keys, email setup,
billing, signing, consent or live validation still require owner action.
Complete independently authorized work before handing off; do not request approvals
again when already granted. Never request secret keys in chat.
Continue sequential milestone delivery: test, report results and outstanding manual
actions, then obtain owner approval before the next milestone.

